# Thread Sanitizer's suppressions for make test-tsan.
# Only a known benign race inside Apple's frameworks belongs here, each with
# its reason. A race in this repo's code is fixed, never suppressed.

# A block that a parallel loop runs is copied to the heap as the loop
# starts: by Thread Sanitizer's own dispatch_apply, once it has ordered the
# caller's writes, and inside CoreFoundation's concurrent sort, which it
# can't see into. The copy's writes come before every iteration that reads
# the block, but the sanitizer sees no order, and reports the block's heap
# memory, with the copy helper as the top frame of one side. Only the top
# frame matches, so a real race whose stack passes through a copy deeper
# still reports.
race_top:__copy_helper_block_
